iv></div><h2 id=3D"p1-20260311" tabindex=3D"-1">P1-20260311</h2><p>P1-20260=
311 is a new generate 3D model (including image to model, text to model, mu=
ltiview to model) optimized for best-in-class low-poly generation. It deliv=
ers exceptionally refined and accurate geometry even at low face counts, ma=
king it ideal for game assets, stylized assets, and lightweight 3D workflow=
s.</p><h3 id=3D"key-features" tabindex=3D"-1">Key Features</h3><ul><li><str=
ong>Optimized Low-Poly Generation</strong>: Produces clean, refined geometr=
y specifically designed for low face count models</li><li><strong>High-Qual=
ity Topology</strong>: Delivers accurate mesh structure even with minimal p=
olygon budgets</li><li><strong>Multi-Input Support</strong>: Compatible wit=
h image, text, and multiview inputs</li><li><strong>Ideal Use Cases</strong=
>: Game assets, stylized 3D content, mobile-optimized models, AR/VR applica=
tions</li><li><strong>Fast Generation</strong>: ~2s mesh generation with st=
ructured topology. Texture generation will add additional processing time.<=
/li></ul><h3 id=3D"parameter-support" tabindex=3D"-1">Parameter Support</h3=
><p>P1-20260311 supports most standard generation parameters with the follo=
wing exceptions. Only the parameters listed below are supported. If you pas=
s any parameters not listed below, the API will return an error. Please che=
ck your request carefully.</p><h4 id=3D"common-parameters-all-input-types" =
tabindex=3D"-1">Common Parameters (All Input Types)</h4><p>These parameters=
 are supported for all input types (image_to_model, text_to_model, multivie=
w_to_model):</p><ul><li><code>model_version</code>: Should always be <code>=
P1-20260311</code>.</li><li><code>model_seed</code> (Optional): This is the=
 random seed for model generation. The seed controls the geometry generatio=
n process, ensuring identical models when the same seed is used. This param=
eter is an integer and is randomly chosen if not set.</li><li><code>face_li=
mit</code> (Optional): Limits the number of faces on the output model. If t=
his option is not set, the face limit will be adaptively determined. The ra=
nge should be <code>48</code> ~ <code>20000</code>.</li><li><code>texture</=
code> (Optional): A boolean option to enable texturing. The default value i=
s <code>true</code>, set <code>false</code> to get a base model without any=
 textures.</li><li><code>pbr</code> (Optional): A boolean option to enable =
pbr. The default value is <code>true</code>, set <code>false</code> to get =
a model without pbr. If this option is set to <code>true</code>, <code>text=
ure</code> will be ignored and used as <code>true</code>.</li><li><code>tex=
ture_seed</code> (Optional): This is the random seed for texture generation=
. Using the same seed will produce identical textures. This parameter is an=
 integer and is randomly chosen if not set. If you want a model with differ=
ent textures, please use same <code>model_seed</code> and different <code>t=
exture_seed</code>.</li><li><code>texture_quality</code> (Optional): This p=
arameter controls the texture quality. <code>detailed</code> provides high-=
resolution textures, resulting in more refined and realistic representation=
 of intricate parts. This option is ideal for models where fine details are=
 crucial for visual fidelity. The default value is <code>standard</code>.</=
li><li><code>auto_size</code> (Optional): Automatically scale the model to =
real-world dimensions, with the unit in meters. The default value is <code>=
false</code>.</li><li><code>compress</code> (Optional): Specifies the compr=
ession type to apply to the texture. Available values are: <ul><li><code>ge=
ometry</code>: Applies geometry-based compression to optimize the output. Y=
ou need to decompress the output model to use it in most model edition soft=
ware if you choose this value. By default, we use <code>meshopt</code> comp=
ression.</li></ul></li><li><code>export_uv</code> (Optional): Controls whet=
her UV unwrapping is performed during generation. The default value is <cod=
e>true</code>. When set to <code>false</code>, generation speed is signific=
antly improved and model size is reduced. UV unwrapping will be handled dur=
ing the texturing stage.</li></ul><h4 id=3D"image-to-model-specific-paramet=
ers" tabindex=3D"-1">Image to Model Specific Parameters</h4><ul><li><code>t=
ype</code>: This field must be set to <code>image_to_model</code>.</li><li>=
<code>file</code>: Specifies the image input. The suggested resolution shou=
ld be more than 256 x 256px. <ul><li><code>type</code>: Indicates the file =
type. Although currently not validated, specifying the correct file type is=
 strongly advised.</li><li><code>file_token</code>: The identifier you get =
from upload, please read <a href=3D"https://platform.tripo3d.ai/docs/upload=
">Docs/Upload</a>. Mutually exclusive with <code>url</code> and <code>objec=
t</code>.</li><li><code>url</code>: A direct URL to the image. Supports JPE=
G and PNG formats with maximum size of 20MB. Mutually exclusive with <code>=
